WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.412
Your stars, your best times and your open maps now come from your own rides.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.169
Every map has three stars: finish, a top three against the medium pack, and beat

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.588
your best. Once earned, never lost.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.669
The next unlock is the first locked map you can work on now. For the mid rider it is

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:33.697
Neon Docklands, and Race Setup on Old Town Criterium names the same goal.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:43.997
For the veteran it is Col du Granit: earn three stars on Dolomites. A best of over

00:00:43.997 --> 00:00:45.908
an hour reads in minutes.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.100
A map a ride opened is open everywhere, and Race Setup is ready for it.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.149
On a phone the path is one column. From a laptop, the star rules sit beside it.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.726
What the tests prove: the next unlock case by case, your maps through the API, and

00:01:19.726 --> 00:01:21.751
every screen that shows them.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
